@startuml Payment Declined Flow
!theme plain
title Stripe Payment - Authorization Declined Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer as C
participant "OrderController" as OC
participant "EventDispatcher" as ED
participant "StripeCheckoutReturnHandler" as SCRH
participant "Stripe API" as S
database "Database" as DB

== Scenario A: Stripe Handles Decline Internally ==

note over C, S #FFFFCC
  **Most Common Case**
  Stripe Checkout handles card declines
  internally without redirecting to shop
end note

C -> S: Enter card details on Stripe Checkout
activate S

S -> S: Attempt authorization
note right of S
  Card issuer declines:
  - Insufficient funds
  - Card expired
  - Fraud suspected
  - etc.
end note

S --> C: "Your card was declined.\nPlease try a different payment method."
deactivate S

note over C
  Customer stays on Stripe Checkout
  Can try another card
  Or click "Back" (cancel flow)
end note

== Scenario B: Redirect with Failed Status ==

note over C, S #FFEEEE
  **Less Common Case**
  Some failure scenarios redirect
  back to success_url with failed payment
end note

C -> S: Complete 3DS / processing
S -> S: Payment fails after redirect initiated
S --> C: Redirect to success_url\n(with session_id)

C -> OC: GET /order?fnc=checkoutSuccess\n&session_id=cs_xxx&contract_id=xxx&contract_token=xxx
activate OC

OC -> ED: dispatch(StripeCheckoutReturnEvent)
activate ED

ED -> SCRH: handle(event)
activate SCRH

SCRH -> SCRH: Validate contract_token ✓
SCRH -> DB: Load contract ✓

SCRH -> S: checkout.sessions.retrieve(cs_xxx)
activate S
S --> SCRH: Session {\n  payment_status: 'unpaid',\n  status: 'open'\n}
deactivate S

alt Payment Intent exists
  SCRH -> S: paymentIntents.retrieve(pi_xxx)
  activate S
  S --> SCRH: PaymentIntent {\n  status: 'requires_payment_method',\n  last_payment_error: {\n    code: 'card_declined',\n    message: 'Your card was declined'\n  }\n}
  deactivate S
end

SCRH -> SCRH: Payment NOT successful

SCRH -> ED: context.set('paymentFailed', true)\ncontext.set('error', 'Your card was declined')\ncontext.set('declineCode', 'card_declined')
deactivate SCRH

ED --> OC: Event processed
deactivate ED

OC -> OC: Check context for errors

OC --> C: Redirect to payment page\nwith error message
deactivate OC

== Result ==

note over C, DB #FFEEEE
  ❌ No order created
  ❌ Payment not captured
  ⚠️ Contract remains PENDING
  ✅ Customer sees error message
  ✅ Customer can retry payment
end note

== Payment Intent Status Reference ==

note over S
  **PaymentIntent.status values:**

  | Status | Meaning | Action |
  |--------|---------|--------|
  | succeeded | Payment OK | Create order |
  | processing | Async processing | Wait for webhook |
  | requires_payment_method | Declined | Show error |
  | requires_action | 3DS needed | Redirect |
  | requires_confirmation | Needs confirm | Confirm |
  | canceled | Canceled | Show error |

  **Common decline codes:**
  - card_declined
  - insufficient_funds
  - expired_card
  - incorrect_cvc
  - processing_error
  - fraudulent
end note

@enduml
